-- A lectern is one of the Custom PDF objects on the console. It only displays.
-- The rules panel decides what goes on it and does the swapping, so this script
-- carries nothing but the page jump.
--
-- Two things were established in game and shape the whole design:
--
-- 1. setCustomObject does not work on a Custom PDF. getCustomObject returns an
--    empty table on these objects -- Custom PDF is absent from the nine types
--    the API documents -- so writing pdf_url into it changes nothing and the
--    reload that follows simply restores the original document. The url has to
--    be read and written through getJSON instead, which the panel does.
--
-- 2. Buttons cannot be placed on the cover. getBoundsNormalized reports a box
--    of roughly 6.2 x 8.0 units against artwork about half that size, so there
--    is no reliable anchor. Hence the real plates on the panel, and hence the
--    page jump living on the right-click menu rather than on the object.

-- The page belongs to the document in front of you rather than to the panel,
-- so it is driven from the lectern. Book.setPage takes effect immediately, no
-- reload involved, which is why this one does work in place.
function rulesLecternGoToPage(playerColor)
  local book = self.Book
  if not book then return end
  Player[playerColor].showInputDialog('Page number', tostring(book.getPage()),
    function(text)
      local page = tonumber(text)
      if not page then return end
      page = math.floor(page)
      if not book.setPage(page) then
        broadcastToColor('This document has no page ' .. page .. '.',
          playerColor, { 1, 0.5, 0.5 })
      end
    end)
end

function onLoad()
  self.clearContextMenu()
  self.addContextMenuItem('Go to page', rulesLecternGoToPage)
end
